# The saas control plane is its own git repository living inside this one, and
# its worktrees get checked out beside it as `saas-<topic>`. They are foreign
# checkouts, so `git add` on one writes a gitlink to a commit this repo has
# never heard of. Ignored as a class rather than a line per worktree: the
# per-worktree entries this replaces lived in .git/info/exclude, which is
# local-only, so every new worktree showed up as untracked work to anyone who
# had not hand-patched their own copy.
/saas
/saas-*/

.pnp.*
.yarn/*
.yarn/install-state.gz
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions
/.yarn/install-state.gz
# Firebase Hosting's per-deploy upload cache. The path was
# /website-astro-v2/.firebase/... until the directory was renamed to website/,
# after which nothing matched and the cache was committed by accident.
# Directory-wide, so a differently-named site cache cannot slip through again.
/website/.firebase/
app/frontend/debug_trace**
.rebase-dev-port
.rebase/
.test-npmrc
packages/forms/.yarn/

# Scratch and debug artifacts (prevent root pollution)
/scratch.*
/test-*.js
/test_*.js
/test-*.ts
/test_*.ts
/fix-*.js
/fix_*.js
/fix-*.cjs
/fix_*.cjs
/fix-*.mjs
/fix-*.ts
/migration-*.ts
/patch_*.js
*.diff
/refactor-*.mjs

# The same scratch scripts, ANYWHERE — not only at the root.
#
# AGENT.md bans one-off scripts in the repo root *and inside any package
# directory*, but every pattern above is root-anchored, so only half of that was
# enforced. `website/.v.mjs` — a throwaway Playwright screenshot script writing
# into an agent scratchpad — sailed past all of them and sat untracked in the
# tree, one `git add -A` away from being committed. Unanchored on purpose.
**/scratch.*
**/fix-*.mjs
**/patch-*.mjs
**/.v.mjs

# Live session state from the `impeccable` skill: a PID/port heartbeat
# (`{"pid":…,"port":…,"lastBeat":…}`), rewritten while a session runs. Not
# source, and it had already been `git add`ed once.
.impeccable/
/eslint-errors*.json
/graph.json
/lerna-debug.log
/*.txt
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/PUBLISHING.md
!/LICENSE
yarn.lock
package-lock.json
app/uploads/
.rebase-dev-url

*.d.ts
!packages/admin/src/editor/markdown-it-plugins.d.ts

# Hand-written declaration files. The blanket rule above exists for *generated*
# declarations, and it silently swallowed these — which is worse than it sounds:
# `react-absent.d.ts` is what makes `pnpm check:baas-types` mean anything, and without
# it in the tree the guard resolved `react` to the real @types/react and passed while
# proving nothing. A file importing React.ReactNode into the BaaS graph produced zero
# errors. Anything hand-written and load-bearing needs a line here.
!e2e/baas-typecheck/stubs/*.d.ts
!app/config/*.d.ts
!packages/cli/templates/template/config/*.d.ts
# `examples/firebase` declares `*.css` here, so `import "./index.css"` typechecks.
# Untracked, it passed locally and failed `check:examples` on a clean checkout
# with TS2882 — the same silent swallow, found the first run CI got that far.
!examples/firebase/src/env.d.ts
# The `virtual:starlight/*` module shims the website's own build needs.
!website/src/starlight.d.ts
# The API-surface gate's fixture barrel. Untracked, `pnpm test:gates` passes
# locally off files CI never receives and the gate's own tests prove nothing.
!scripts/test/fixtures/**/*.d.ts

